{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/504043-kindred-2-0-vs-hall-of-mirrors","id":504043,"title":"Kindred 2.0 vs Hall of Mirrors","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-05T05:14:12-07:00","id":504043,"title":"Kindred 2.0 vs Hall of Mirrors","content":"Not an important question - quirky at best. It Requiem 1.0, Vampires became blurred in mirrors, cameras, etc.... In Requiem 2.0 it says that the beast instictively keeps the vampire turned from mirrors, cameras, etc... so they appear normal, but simply never get direct line of sight.<br /> <br /> So the challenge then - the Hall of Mirrors. What happens? Does the vampires face implode as the beast goes insane trying to turn the Kindred away from EVERY mirror? Does it discourage them strongly from entering - creating a minor 'danger sense'? Do the lights in the hall seem to flicker via the beast playing with the light switch remotely to prevent clear images? Or does the beast cause the appropriately reflecting mirrors to crack 'just enough' so that the image becomes incomprehensable?<br /> <br /> Like I said, an amusing one to answer at best. Have fun forum peoples!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T06:26:18-07:00","id":504096,"title":"","content":"They'll be reflected properly in one or two mirrors, but it will never be the ones anybody is looking at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T21:07:37-07:00","id":504991,"title":"","content":"Who says the reflections in the mirror match up to reality? All the reflections are blurred or looking the wrong way, even if the vampire is staring straight into one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1230-thenagain","name":"thenagain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T21:38:44-07:00","id":505035,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about that, but if I recall correctly the book does state that a reflection can be 'pinned down' so to speak. So you may think, 'That man has no reflection! VAMPIRE!' But upon closer inspection, with you vaguely in front of him and a mirror vaguely behind him, you'd be reassured that he, indeed, does have a reflection and thus isn't a vampire at all, and instead a werewolf.<br /> <br /> So then I was thinking about <i>Hell of Mirrors</i> from Edogawa Ranpo. In the story a man obsessed with mirrors and lenses and his own reflection decides to sort of form a sphere for himself, with a mirrored inside. And I thought to myself, what would a vampire see? Well, considering my theory on the first question, they would see their reflection, and to see what that was like, I saw <a href=\"https://youtu.be/zRP82omMX0g\" target=\"_blank\">this </a>weirdly interesting video. But then I thought, what would a Hollow see? What do you see in a sphere of mirrors when there you have no reflection?<br /> <br /> And from there I started wondering about the Hollows, and that perhaps there was a rare bloodline of vampires descended from a Reflection, who perhaps managed to trap their Hollow in a room such as this.<br /> <br /> Which led me to remembering <i>The Strix Chronicle Anthology</i>, which might be renamed by now on DriveThruRPG. There's a story in there I never got, <i>Fading Away</i> by Matthew McFarland. I appreciate it maybe a fiction from the first edition, but if it is not does anyone know what happened to the protagonist, the why of it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-06-2015, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}